{"title":"BeFS","slug":"BeFS","html":"<div class=\"wk-navbox\">\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-title\">\n<p><a data-wiki=\"File Systems\" href=\"#/library/File_Systems\">Filesystems</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Virtual Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"VFS\" href=\"#/library/VFS\">VFS</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Disk Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT\">FAT</a> <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/fat_12\">12</a>/<a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/fat_16\">16</a>/<a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/fat_32\">32</a>, <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/vfat\">VFAT</a>, <a data-wiki=\"ExFAT\" href=\"#/library/ExFAT\">ExFAT</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Ext2\" href=\"#/library/Ext2\">Ext 2</a>/<a data-wiki=\"Ext3\" href=\"#/library/Ext3\">3</a>/<a data-wiki=\"Ext4\" href=\"#/library/Ext4\">4</a> · <a data-wiki=\"LEAN\" href=\"#/library/LEAN\">LEAN</a> · <a data-wiki=\"HPFS\" href=\"#/library/HPFS\">HPFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"NTFS\" href=\"#/library/NTFS\">NTFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"HFS\" href=\"#/library/HFS\">HFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"HFS+\" href=\"#/library/HFS_plus\">HFS+</a> · <a data-wiki=\"MFS\" href=\"#/library/MFS\">MFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"ReiserFS\" href=\"#/library/ReiserFS\">ReiserFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"FFS (Amiga)\" href=\"#/library/FFS_Amiga\">FFS (Amiga)</a> · <a data-wiki=\"UFS\" href=\"#/library/UFS\">FFS (BSD)</a>/<a data-wiki=\"UFS\" href=\"#/library/UFS\">UFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"BeFS\" href=\"#/library/BeFS\">BeFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"BFS\" href=\"#/library/BFS\">BFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"XFS\" href=\"#/library/XFS\">XFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"SFS\" href=\"#/library/SFS\">SFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"ZDSFS\" href=\"#/library/ZDSFS\">ZDSFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"ZFS\" href=\"#/library/ZFS\">ZFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"USTAR\" href=\"#/library/USTAR\">USTAR</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">CD/DVD Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"ISO 9660\" href=\"#/library/ISO_9660\">ISO 9660</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Joliet\" href=\"#/library/Joliet\">Joliet</a> · <a data-wiki=\"UDF\" href=\"#/library/UDF\">UDF</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\"><a href=\"#/library?cat=Network_Filesystems\">Network Filesystems</a></span> <a data-wiki=\"NFS\" href=\"#/library/NFS\">NFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"RFS\" href=\"#/library/RFS\">RFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"AFS\" href=\"#/library/AFS\">AFS</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Flash Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"JFFS2\" href=\"#/library/JFFS2\">JFFS2</a> · <a data-wiki=\"YAFFS\" href=\"#/library/YAFFS\">YAFFS</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-note wk-stub\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Stub</span></p>\n<p>This page on the OSDev Wiki is a stub: it covers the basics but is not complete.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"about_befs\">About BeFS</h2>\n<p><strong>BeFS</strong> is the new filesystem for the Be Operating system. It is very much like the MacOS Filesystem, supporting multiple forks in a 64bit filesystem. One very useful feature it shares with the AmigaOS FFS is the ability for an application to set a \"notify callback\", i.e. being notified when a file or directory changes.</p>\n<h2 id=\"see_also\">See Also</h2>\n<h3 id=\"external_links\">External Links</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.nobius.org/~dbg/practical-file-system-design.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\">Practical File System Design</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"about_befs","text":"About BeFS","level":2},{"id":"see_also","text":"See Also","level":2},{"id":"external_links","text":"External Links","level":3}],"categories":["Filesystems"],"rating":null,"flags":["stub"],"words":162,"summary":"BeFS is the new filesystem for the Be Operating system. It is very much like the MacOS Filesystem, supporting multiple forks in a 64bit filesystem. One very useful